    <p>{{ site.name }} (“we,” “us,” or “our”) respects your privacy. This policy explains what information we collect through <a href="{{ site.url }}">{{ site.url }}</a> and related contact channels, how we use it, and the choices available to you.</p>

    <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-top:40px;">Information we collect</h2>
    <p>We may collect information you voluntarily submit through our contact form, email, phone, or newsletter signup, including your name, email address, phone number, company, and a description of your inquiry. We may also receive limited technical data such as browser type, device information, and approximate location from standard server or analytics logs.</p>

    <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-top:40px;">How we use information</h2>
    <p>We use submitted information to respond to inquiries, evaluate whether we can assist with a matter, schedule consultations, improve the website, and comply with legal obligations. We do not sell your personal information.</p>

    <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-top:40px;">Sharing</h2>
    <p>We may share information with service providers who help us operate the website or communications tools (for example, form processors or email providers), and when required by law or to protect our rights. Those providers are expected to use the information only to perform services for us.</p>

    <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-top:40px;">Confidentiality notice</h2>
    <p>Submitting information through this website does not create an attorney-client relationship. Please do not send sensitive or confidential matter details until we have confirmed an engagement in writing.</p>

    <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-top:40px;">Retention &amp; security</h2>
    <p>We retain inquiry information as needed to respond and for ordinary business and compliance records. We use reasonable administrative and technical safeguards, but no method of transmission over the internet is completely secure.</p>

